.* DSPMSGD: a message file's descriptions (LIST), what to show of one
.* (SELECT) and the details: its text (TEXT), its fields (FIELDS) and
.* its attributes (ATTRS).
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Quartz Systems 2026
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=IDCL BASETYPE='CHAR 7'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TEXTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 70'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=LINECL BASETYPE='CHAR 77'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=SELCL BASETYPE='CHAR 2'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=WIDCL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=SYSNM CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=MSGID CLASS=IDCL.
:VAR NAME=MSGF CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=MSGFLIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=TEXT1 CLASS=TEXTCL.
:VAR NAME=TEXT2 CLASS=LINECL.
:VAR NAME=SEL CLASS=SELCL.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=ID CLASS=IDCL.
:VAR NAME=IDTEXT CLASS=TEXTCL.
:VAR NAME=LINE CLASS=LINECL.
:VAR NAME=SEV CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=LOGPRB CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='*NO'.
:VAR NAME=DFTPGM CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='*NONE'.
:VAR NAME=DFTLIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=LEVEL CLASS=TEXTCL.
:VAR NAME=ALROPT CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='*NO'.
:VAR NAME=DMPLST CLASS=TEXTCL VALUE='*NONE'.
:VAR NAME=RPYTYPE CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='*NONE'.
:VAR NAME=VALUES CLASS=TEXTCL VALUE='*NONE'.
:VAR NAME=DFTRPY CLASS=TEXTCL VALUE='*NONE'.
:VAR NAME=WID CLASS=WIDCL.
:VAR NAME=POSTO CLASS=IDCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=IDS VARS='OPT ID IDTEXT'.
:LISTDEF NAME=WIDS VARS='OPT WID IDTEXT'.
:LISTDEF NAME=LINES VARS='LINE'.
:KEYL NAME=KEYS HELP=KEYSHLP.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:EKEYL.
:KEYL NAME=WKEYS HELP=KEYSHLP.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F6 ACTION='RETURN 6'.F6=Add
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=LIST KEYL=KEYS HELP=LISTH ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Display Message Descriptions
:DATA DEPTH=3.
:DATAC.Message file . . . . . . . . :   &MSGF.
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.
:DATAC.Library  . . . . . . . . . :     &MSGFLIB.
:EDATAGRP.
:EDATA.
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=IDS SCROLL=YES.
:LISTACT HELP='LIST/OPTIONS' OPTION=5 ENTER='RETURN 5'.5=Display details
:LISTCOL HELP='LIST/OPT' VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/ID' VAR=ID USAGE=OUTPUT.Message ID
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/IDTEXT' VAR=IDTEXT USAGE=OUTPUT.Message Text
:ELIST.
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=WORK KEYL=WKEYS HELP=WORKH ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Work with Message Descriptions
:DATA DEPTH=4.
:DATACOL WIDTH=25.
:DATACOL WIDTH=78.
:DATAC.Message file:   &MSGF.        Library:   &MSGFLIB.
:DATAC.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/POSTO' VAR=POSTO USAGE=INOUT.Position to
:EDATA.
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=WIDS SCROLL=YES.(No message descriptions)
:LISTACT HELP='WORK/OPTIONS' OPTION=2 ENTER='CMD ?CHGMSGD MSGID(&WID.) MSGF(&MSGFLIB./&MSGF.)'.2=Change
:LISTACT HELP='WORK/OPTIONS' OPTION=4 ENTER='CMD RMVMSGD MSGID(&WID.) MSGF(&MSGFLIB./&MSGF.)'.4=Remove
:LISTACT HELP='WORK/OPTIONS' OPTION=5 ENTER='CMD DSPMSGD RANGE(&WID.) MSGF(&MSGFLIB./&MSGF.)'.5=Display details
:LISTACT HELP='WORK/OPTIONS' OPTION=6 ENTER='RETURN 106'.6=Print
:LISTCOL HELP='WORK/OPT' VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/WID' VAR=WID USAGE=OUTPUT.Message ID
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/IDTEXT' VAR=IDTEXT USAGE=OUTPUT.Message Text
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Parameters or command
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=SELECT KEYL=KEYS HELP=SELECTH ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Select Message Details to Display
:DATA DEPTH=6.
:DATAC.Message ID . . . . . . . . . :   &MSGID.
:DATAC.Message file . . . . . . . . :   &MSGF.
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.
:DATAC.Library  . . . . . . . . . :     &MSGFLIB.
:EDATAGRP.
:DATAC.Message text . . . . . . . . :   &TEXT1.
:DATAC.&TEXT2.
:EDATA.
:MENU DEPTH='*'.Select one of the following:
:MENUI HELP='SELECT/OPT1' OPTION=1 ACTION='RETURN 1'.Display message text
:MENUI HELP='SELECT/OPT2' OPTION=2 ACTION='RETURN 2'.Display field data
:MENUI HELP='SELECT/OPT5' OPTION=5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.Display message attributes
:MENUI HELP='SELECT/OPT30' OPTION=30 ACTION='RETURN 30'.All of the above
:EMENU.
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=TEXT KEYL=KEYS HELP=SELECTH ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Display Formatted Message Text
:DATA DEPTH=4.
:DATAC.Message ID . . . . . . . . . :   &MSGID.
:DATAC.Message file . . . . . . . . :   &MSGF.
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.
:DATAC.Library  . . . . . . . . . :     &MSGFLIB.
:EDATAGRP.
:EDATA.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=LINES SCROLL=YES.
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/LINE' VAR=LINE USAGE=OUTPUT.
:ELIST.
:BOTINST.Press Enter to continue.
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=FIELDS KEYL=KEYS HELP=SELECTH ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Display Field Data
:DATA DEPTH=4.
:DATAC.Message ID . . . . . . . . . :   &MSGID.
:DATAC.Message file . . . . . . . . :   &MSGF.
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.
:DATAC.Library  . . . . . . . . . :     &MSGFLIB.
:EDATAGRP.
:EDATA.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=LINES SCROLL=YES.
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/LINE' VAR=LINE USAGE=OUTPUT.Field     Data Type          Length
:ELIST.
:BOTINST.Press Enter to continue.
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=ATTRS KEYL=KEYS HELP=SELECTH ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Display Message Attributes
:DATA DEPTH='*'.
:DATAC.Message ID . . . . . . . . . :   &MSGID.
:DATAC.Message file . . . . . . . . :   &MSGF.
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.
:DATAC.Library  . . . . . . . . . :     &MSGFLIB.
:EDATAGRP.
:DATAC.
:DATAC.Severity . . . . . . . . . . :   &SEV.
:DATAC.
:DATAC.Log problem  . . . . . . . . :   &LOGPRB.
:DATAC.
:DATAC.Default program  . . . . . . :   &DFTPGM.
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.
:DATAC.Default library  . . . . . :     &DFTLIB.
:EDATAGRP.
:DATAC.
:DATAC.Message level  . . . . . . . :   &LEVEL.
:DATAC.
:DATAC.Alert option . . . . . . . . :   &ALROPT.
:DATAC.
:DATAC.Data to be dumped  . . . . . :   &DMPLST.
:DATAC.
:DATAC.Reply type . . . . . . . . . :   &RPYTYPE.
:DATAC.
:DATAC.Valid reply values . . . . . :   &VALUES.
:DATAC.
:DATAC.Default reply value  . . . . :   &DFTRPY.
:EDATA.
:BOTINST.Press Enter to continue.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WORKH.Work with Message Descriptions - Help
:P.The descriptions of a message file: change, remove or look at one.
ADDMSGD adds another.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=LISTH.Display Message Descriptions - Help
:P.The descriptions in a message file, by identifier. Type 5 next to
one to choose what to see of it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SELECTH.Message description - Help
:P.Option 1 shows the message's first and second level texts, 2 the
substitution fields its data fills, 5 its severity, logging, dump
list and replies; 30 shows each in turn.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=KEYSHLP.Function keys - Help
:P.F3 leaves the display, F12 goes back one display.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='LIST/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ID'.Message ID
:P.The message ID of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/IDTEXT'.Message Text
:P.The text of the message.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LIST/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.5=Display details
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display details it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/POSTO'.Position to
:P.Type the position to.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WORK/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/WID'.Message ID
:P.The message ID of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WORK/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it. The Change
Message Description (CHGMSGD) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.4=Remove
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to remove it. The Remove
Message Description (RMVMSGD) command runs for the entry.
:PT.5=Display details
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display details it. The
Display Message Description (DSPMSGD) command runs for the entry.
:PT.6=Print
:PD.Type 6 next to an entry and press Enter to print it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SELECT/OPT1'.Display message text
:P.Option 1. Display message text.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SELECT/OPT2'.Display field data
:P.Option 2. Display field data.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SELECT/OPT5'.Display message attributes
:P.Option 5. Display message attributes.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SELECT/OPT30'.All of the above
:P.Option 30. All of the above.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LINE'.LINE
:P.The line description.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
